  "2026-11-02T09:41:58.054Z",pi-glm,"Duplicate GH278 provenance reconciled. Both owners were identified from the failing run 41407648593 ('import plan is not idempotent — 1 duplicate provenance tag(s)') and a tracker scan: the cited-evidence inspection feature (kept as sole owner — PR 278 delivers it and its record declares that tag for exact sync identity) and the SDK evidence-fragments record (de-owned). The de-owned record's gh: tag was removed with 'pm update --remove-tags', a related dependency now links it to the owning feature record, its delivery knowledge (body, comments, files, tests, close evidence) is untouched and its status stays closed. Measurement — before: failing run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/41407648593 (2026-11-02T07:38Z, 'Preview GitHub to pm plan' step). After: the same gated dry-run the scheduled workflow runs (pm-github 2026.10.19 as pinned by the reusable workflow) passes against this branch's tracker: fetched 10, planned 10, import 6, update 4, skip 0, provenance-indexed 11, gate verified with no duplicate provenance tag. The command is linked as a passing test; its pm-test receipt runs in pm's isolated seeded workspace, so the reconciliation numbers here come from the direct dry-run against this checkout. GitHub API budget was checked before measuring (core remaining above the 1500 floor). Guard unchanged; item stays open for orchestrator close after merge."
  "2026-11-06T15:13:30.235Z",codex-sol,"Rechecking issue #288 at main 1a8ce23d8cb17a867ae0205bffc05f4e10d49f39. Main already includes the GH278 metadata repair from PR #292: pm-web-5sx6 is the sole importer owner and pm-web-cnhi keeps its related dependency and delivery evidence. Scheduled sync run 42183873938 succeeded on this exact main SHA, including gated preview, import, repeat no-op, privacy and strict health. Plan: reproduce with pm-github 2026.10.19 and a real disposable SDK tracker, retain duplicate-negative-control and read-only repeat evidence, then submit an evidence-only closure PR without product or workflow changes."
  "2026-11-06T15:13:43.992Z",codex-sol,"Rechecking #288 at main 1a8ce23d8cb17a867ae0205bffc05f4e10d49f39. PR #292 already repaired duplicate GH278 metadata, retaining both records and delivery evidence. Scheduled sync 42183873938 succeeded on this SHA, including guarded preview/import and repeat no-op. Reproduce with pm-github 2026.10.19 and a disposable real SDK tracker; evidence-only closure PR, no product changes."
  "2026-11-06T15:22:05.545Z",codex-sol,"Historical pm-github 2026.10.19 accepts the complete 204-item corpus (19 provenance identities). In a disposable copy, SDK addTags on pm-web-cnhi restores the original 1 duplicate / 0 missing provenance / 0 conflicting targets refusal; document/history hashes stay unchanged across refusal. SDK removeTags restores acceptance. Two full real GitHub gated dry-run JSON plans match exactly (0 creates, 11 updates, 0 skips) without document/history writes. Existing workflow security/update tests pass 8/8, also linked and rerun with pm test --run --only-last --progress. npm and Bun release:check both pass typechecks, lint, zero-duplication and 936 docstring declarations, then fail closed at unavailable test PostgreSQL; CI supplies the service. No gate or threshold was changed."
  "2026-11-06T15:24:08.184Z",codex-sol,"All four retained verification scenarios now pass, including a newly initialized no-git tracker created through PmClient: duplicate identity refuses without item/history changes, then SDK tag removal accepts. The documentation fixture also passes standalone TypeScript checking. Main is already fixed by PR #292, verified on 1a8ce23d8cb17a867ae0205bffc05f4e10d49f39 and successful normal scheduled run 42183873938. This branch changes only the existing tracking item/history and verification documentation; no implementation fix is warranted. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; releasing only the codex-sol claim. The closure PR will carry final-head CI and review results."
  "2026-11-06T15:58:12.881Z",codex-sol,"Thirty-minute post-push cutoff for PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/pull/304 at remote head 2c5c4de490f1baf568ef93d09106ed8663949739. CI https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42243131106: Node 22 full npm release gate passed, full Bun release gate still running; Node 26 queued. CodeQL https://github.com/unbraind/pm-web/actions/runs/42243131075 passed. CodeRabbit request is queued through the required shared queue, with zero completed rounds and no reviewed-head receipt; zero unresolved threads and zero unvoted bot comments. Sourcery reports a quota limit (guide only), Greptile reports expired trial, and cubic is neutral; none is approval. Final-head fixture passed all four scenarios; isolated-Git focused tests passed 8/8. No product changes or fixes were needed because main already repaired #288. This pending-results receipt is retained locally for the next fix push as required by the review-loop rule; no standalone PM-only push."
  "2026-11-06T20:10:30.943Z",codex-sol,"Resumed PR #304 after CodeRabbit reviewed f04a045: four valid reproducibility gaps (bind corpus to the recorded SHA, enforce archive digest before extraction, verify actual SDK/CLI versions, exercise the full gated write entrypoint), plus three supporting improvements (post-repair Git apply, pre-repair preservation baseline, nonempty provider/gate receipts). Retaining the already-fixed product scope; strengthening only the documented real-tracker verification. Prior receipt commit is already on origin. Will push every new receipt and fix, then reply to all threads in one batch and requeue."
  "2026-11-06T20:28:00.615Z",codex-sol,"Review regressions: five refusal controls (wrong commit, dirty checkout, actual SDK 2026.11.5, actual CLI 2026.11.5 with pinned SDK, altered archive) fail against original f04a045 documentation and pass against the revised preflight/setup; two must-allow controls (exact historical identity and archive) pass. The real historical CLI is verified against the installed source bytes. The Git-backed duplicate control deliberately makes issue 288 stale, proving writes would occur if admitted: bypassing only the importer pre-write verifyImportIdempotency call makes the new unchanged-item/history assertion fail, while leaving the exported verifier intact. The mutation is restored in finally. Typecheck and lint pass; the first lint attempt traversed nested disposable worktrees, which have been moved outside the package without changing lint policy. The final pristine fixture and changelog checks are completing before the fix push."
  "2026-11-06T20:28:47.250Z",codex-sol,"Final review-fix validation: the restored, unmodified historical package passes all four documented scenarios on clean source 1a8ce23d8cb17a867ae0205bffc05f4e10d49f39. This includes real Git-backed non-dry-run duplicate refusal with no item/history writes, successful apply that repairs a deliberately stale issue 288, complete original delivery metadata/relationship preservation and pre-repair history prefixes for both GH278 records, nonempty bounded provider receipts, and a fresh no-git SDK tracker. Five refusal regressions plus two allow controls pass; original f04a045 fails the five refusal regressions. Bypassing the importer pre-write check alone fails the new no-write assertion; finally restoration is verified by the full passing rerun. Fixture standalone TypeScript, package typecheck and lint pass. Prior f04a045 CI completed successfully on Node 22/26 and CodeQL; the new fix push needs fresh CI and CodeRabbit evidence. All four inline findings and all three nitpicks are addressed. Final review/CI outcomes will be recorded in PR #304 and the final summary; every local commit will be pushed under the updated rule."
  "2026-11-09T06:49:02.601Z",codex-agent,"Continuation review: retained the existing main merge and tracker claim after inspecting local/remote history and PR 304. All review-thread/comment pages are complete: one unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c60vfjH; latest CodeRabbit review has no outside-diff findings. The no-Git control lacks a pre-initialization Git boundary check. Add a fail-closed directory check and execute regression controls against the documented function, including a behavioral revert. No review replies or resolutions."
  "2026-11-09T06:51:35.874Z",codex-agent,"PRRT_kwDOSZgR5c60vfjH fixed in the documented plain setup: require Git status 128 plus the exact C-locale no-repository diagnostic, reject process errors, and check both before and after real SDK initialization. Regression command node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/gated-sync-verification.test.ts passes 4/4 (plain allow; worktree, bare and corrupt-metadata refusal before tracker writes). Behavioral revert in a disposable copy removed only the two boundary-check calls: plain allow passed, all three refusal controls failed with Missing expected rejection. Restoring the calls passed 4/4. The reviewed checkout was never mutated by the proof. The linked focused workflow/identity/boundary command passes 16/16 through pm test --run --only-last --progress. Whole PR diff self-review found no further instance; latest review has no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-11-09T06:55:47.532Z",codex-agent,"Final local review-round evidence: boundary suite 4/4 on repo-pinned SDK 2026.11.5 and independently installed historical SDK 2026.11.2; linked boundary/workflow/identity tests 16/16. npm run release:check and bun run release:check were attempted with isolated Git identity; after preserving ignored scratch fixture copies outside the source scan, both pass typecheck, lint, duplication 0% (0/63830 lines, 348 sources), docstrings (934 declarations in 204 files), build and test TypeScript compilation, then stop at mandatory throwaway PostgreSQL preflight (database unavailable). No thresholds or skip policy changed; full release gates are not certified locally. Rebuilt committed dist and frontend artifacts have zero drift. CI-pinned extension installation removes local host-version skew; pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers passes 10/10, zero warnings; merge report has zero unresolved receipts. Release changelog-date and publish-attestation gates pass. Current-head CI is required after pushing the retained main merge and this fix; results remain available on PR 304. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; releasing only this agent claim. No review thread replies, resolutions, mentions, merge or release."
